      "content": "thanks for looking into that. but it's more than just sound quality. if they're using the plants as diffusers to manage ambient noise, that's one thing, but what if the goal is the opposite? if you have a high-density leaf pattern acting as a parabolic reflector, you could actually funnel sound from a specific seat toward a single point. if the city or some agency wanted to listen in without installing actual tech, they'd just need someone to set the plants up according to an acoustic map. it's not a \"leap\" if the physics actually support it—it's just a clever way to hide the hardware in plain sight. can you explain how a specific arrangement of reflective leaf surfaces could theoretically be used to focus sound waves toward a central collection point?",
